Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?vulkan=20:=20R52b=20=E2=80=94=20S-X8=20mul=5Fmm?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20PACKED=20tile=20decode,=20and=20integer=20MMQ=20reachable=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?under=20coopmat=20(opt-in)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

R52 proved the S-X8 prefill deficit on a KHR_coopmat device is not a missing integer kernel:
both S-X8 and q8_0 run the coopmat mul_mm f16 path, so the gap is in the S-X8 tile decode.
This lane fixes that decode at the root and, per HQ, makes the integer-MMQ alternative
measurable on the same binary instead of assumed dead.

1. PACKED TILE DECODE (mul_mm_funcs.glsl, load_a_to_shmem, DATA_A_SX8 branch).
   The shipped arm re-reads the qh/ql planes once per WEIGHT — 8 qh + 8 ql byte loads for the
   8 weights one invocation owns (LOAD_VEC_A = 8), 2 VMEM ops per weight, against q8_0's 0.5.
   On a 128x32 A-tile that is 8192 byte loads per BK step feeding 524,288 MACs: the decode is
   1/128 of the arithmetic and still gates the shape, because VMEM issue rate is the ceiling.
   The packed arm calls sx8_levels4() — already in types.glsl since lane-230/R46, four weights
   from three byte reads, one level per byte lane — for 6 byte reads instead of 16. Same
   sx8_range(), same level values, same rlo + step * level, same shmem slots: bit-identical
   by construction. r52b-evidence/30-packed-decode-proof.py checks the helper against
   sx8_level() (ggml-quants.c:2404) over all 2^24 byte triples, 0 mismatches.

   Two SPIR-V variants, one binary, chosen at pipeline creation in all THREE arms of
   ggml_vk_load_shaders (coopmat, fp16, else) — the dot2_f16 shape. A specialization constant
   was refused: the mul_mm spec vector is positional and a 13th entry would land on
   constantID 12 (SHMEM_STRIDE_PAD) for every type on non-Intel devices.
   GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MM_PACKED=0|1 overrides the RDNA3 device probe either way.

2. MMQ UNDER COOPMAT, OPT-IN (GGML_ARIFI_MMQ_UNDER_COOPMAT=1, default OFF).
   mul_mmq.comp is a scalar integer-dot shader, not a coopmat one, and its SPIR-V is compiled
   and linked on every build regardless of device class — so the coopmat arm can register the
   very same modules the fp16 arm does. No routing code changed:
   ggml_vk_get_mul_mat_mat_pipeline() already routes on is_empty() alone. Scoped to q8_0 and
   S-X8, the pair under measurement.

3. TEST COVERAGE (tests/test-backend-ops.cpp). Every S-X8 MUL_MAT row in the sweep was n <= 8,
   which is mat-vec territory: nothing checked the S-X8 mul_mm tile decode at a prefill width.
   Adds m=17408, n=512, k=5120 for SX8 and Q8_0.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-243 R52b S-X8 coopmat mul_mm decode, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: diagnostic only (one shape, receipts); HQ benches quiet (target: 4B S-X8 pp128 from ~380 toward q8_0's ~495 t/s)
Lane: lane-243
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
